window.NEWSTEXT = {"sections":[{"id":"cover-story","name":"カバーストーリー","kind":"news","blurb":"今週その国で一番の話題"},{"id":"news-brief","name":"今週の短信","kind":"news","blurb":"短いニュース3本"},{"id":"street-talk","name":"街の会話","kind":"dialogue","blurb":"現地の友人同士の日常会話"},{"id":"life-column","name":"暮らしのコラム","kind":"blog","blurb":"生活・習慣・世相"},{"id":"buzzword","name":"今週のことば","kind":"buzzword","blurb":"流行語と時事キーワード"},{"id":"culture","name":"カルチャー案内","kind":"culture","blurb":"料理・音楽・映画・行事"}],"languages":["en","zh","es","fr"],"builtAt":"2026-09-01T08:03:33","issues":[{"issue":{"coverTitle":"新学期の国、暖房の国","coverCopy":"9月最初の週。フランスは1160万人がいっせいに登校し、スペインでは教育現場が限界を訴え、内モンゴルでは9か月に及ぶ暖房が始まった。同じ一週間を、4つの言語はまるで違う言葉で語っている。","editorNote":"創刊号です。硬いニュースだけでなく、街角の会話や暮らしのコラムまで6つのコーナーを4か国ぶん揃えました。読み方は自由ですが、まず「街の会話」から入ると、その国の空気がいちばん早くつかめます。","worldRoundup":[{"language":"en","country":"イギリス","flag":"🇬🇧","text":"食料品の値上がりが再び加速。エネルギー価格の上昇が店頭に及び、家計の話題が一週間を占めた。気象庁は今季の嵐の名前を発表し、テニスではジョコビッチが涙の敗戦。フレディ・マーキュリー生誕80年の週でもあった。"},{"language":"zh","country":"中国","flag":"🇨🇳","text":"上海協力機構の首脳会議が最大の話題。一方、内モンゴルでは9か月続く暖房が全国に先駆けて始まり、丁俊晖がスヌーカー英国オープン初戦を突破。老舗料理店・仿膳飯荘は創業101年と中秋の新作を披露した。"},{"language":"es","country":"スペイン","flag":"🇪🇸","text":"セウタをめぐる緊張が政治の中心に。新学年は教員のストライキと抗議で幕を開け、サッカー協会が女子選手の卵子凍結費用を負担すると発表して議論を呼んだ。9月は映画の公開ラッシュでもある。"},{"language":"fr","country":"フランス","flag":"🇫🇷","text":"1160万人が新学期を迎え、高校での携帯電話禁止が施行。生徒の反応は冷ややかで、制服の試験導入は静かに終了した。書店は年に一度の新刊ラッシュ「ラントレ・リテレール」に突入している。"}],"id":"2026-W36","label":"2026年9月 第1週号","dates":"8/31(月) 〜 9/6(日)","weekStart":"2026-08-31","weekEnd":"2026-09-06"},"articles":[{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"en","country":"イギリス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"en-2026-W36-buzzword","section":"buzzword","kind":"buzzword","title":"Words of the week","titleJa":"今週のことば ― 物価と天気のイギリス英語5語","leadJa":"今週のイギリスの紙面と会話に繰り返し現れた5語。経済ニュースの用語から、パブで飛び交う俗語まで。","category":"語彙","level":"中級","trivia":"cost of living crisis という言い方は2021年以降イギリスで定着し、いまでは政治の争点そのものを指す言葉になっています。単なる「物価高」より重い響きです。"},"entries":[{"term":"cost of living","reading":"","meaning":"生活費・暮らしにかかる費用","note":"食料・光熱費・家賃など生活に要する費用の総体。2021年以降のイギリスではcost of living crisis という形で政治の中心的な争点になっており、ニュースでも日常会話でも省略して「the cost of living」とだけ言えば通じる。","example":"The cost of living is still the biggest issue for voters.","exampleJa":"生活費は依然として有権者にとって最大の争点だ。"},{"term":"quid","reading":"","meaning":"ポンド（通貨の口語表現）","note":"pound のくだけた言い方で、複数形も quid のまま変化しない（five quid）。書き言葉やあらたまった場では使わない。10ポンド札は a tenner、5ポンド札は a fiver。","example":"It cost me forty quid, would you believe.","exampleJa":"40ポンドもしたんだ、信じられる？"},{"term":"year on year","reading":"","meaning":"前年同期比で","note":"経済統計の定型表現で、前年の同じ月・同じ四半期と比べた変化を指す。YoY と略される。前月と比べる場合は month on month。数字を読むニュースでは必ず出てくる。","example":"Prices rose 1.5% year on year in August.","exampleJa":"8月の物価は前年同月比1.5%上昇した。"},{"term":"fair enough","reading":"","meaning":"なるほど・了解・まあいいでしょう","note":"相手の言い分を、完全に賛成はしないまでも受け入れるときの相槌。イギリスの会話では極めて頻繁に使われ、議論を穏やかに閉じる働きをする。冷たく短く言うと「もういい」という打ち切りにもなる。","example":"\"I'd rather not, I'm knackered.\" \"Fair enough.\"","exampleJa":"「やめとくよ、へとへとなんだ」「まあ、そうだよな」"},{"term":"to name a storm","reading":"","meaning":"嵐に名前を付ける","note":"2015年に始まったイギリス気象庁の制度。被害が予想され警報を出す嵐にだけ人名を付ける。名前が付いたというだけで深刻さが伝わるため、named storm は「本気で警戒すべき嵐」を意味する。","example":"The Met Office has named the first storm of the season.","exampleJa":"気象庁は今季最初の嵐に名前を付けた。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"en","country":"イギリス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"en-2026-W36-cover-story","section":"cover-story","kind":"news","title":"Price rises gather pace in UK shops amid higher energy costs","titleJa":"イギリスの店頭で値上がりが加速 ― エネルギー高が食卓を直撃","leadJa":"8月、イギリスの店頭物価の上昇率が2年ぶりの高さになりました。缶詰やパッケージ食品が特に上がり、背景にはエネルギー価格の上昇があります。イギリス人が最も敏感な話題「cost of living（生活費）」の最新報告を、ガーディアン紙の配信記事で読みます。","source":"The Guardian","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/01/price-rises-gather-pace-in-uk-shops-higher-energy-costs","sources":[{"name":"The Guardian (Business)","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/01/price-rises-gather-pace-in-uk-shops-higher-energy-costs"},{"name":"BBC News","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3v0qrz7z25o"}],"category":"経済","level":"上級","trivia":"BRC（英国小売協会）の物価指数は、公式統計より早く出るため「物価の先行指標」として毎月ニュースになります。イギリスでは天気の次に、物価が世間話の定番です。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"The pace of price rises in UK shops rose to its highest level in two years in August, a trade body index shows.","translation":"8月、イギリスの店頭における物価上昇のペースが2年ぶりの高水準に達したことが、業界団体の指数で明らかになった。","words":[{"word":"pace","surface":"pace","meaning":"ペース・速度","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"price rise","surface":"price rises","meaning":"値上がり","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"trade body","surface":"trade body","meaning":"業界団体","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"index","surface":"index","meaning":"指数","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"its highest level in two years は「過去2年で最も高い水準」。in + 期間 は最上級とともに「〜の間で」を表す頻出パターン。"},{"id":2,"original":"Higher energy costs are pushing up the price of food, with AI chip demand making technology more expensive.","translation":"エネルギー費用の上昇が食品価格を押し上げており、AI向け半導体の需要が電子機器を値上がりさせている。","words":[{"word":"push up","surface":"pushing up","meaning":"押し上げる","pos":"句動詞"},{"word":"demand","surface":"demand","meaning":"需要","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"expensive","surface":"expensive","meaning":"高価な","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"with + 名詞 + 現在分詞（with AI chip demand making...）は付帯状況の with。「〜が…している状態で」と、もう一つの事情を添える書き言葉の型。"},{"id":3,"original":"In-store inflation stepped up to 1.5% year on year in August, up from 0.9% in July.","translation":"店頭インフレ率は8月に前年同月比1.5%へと上昇した。7月の0.9%からの上昇である。","words":[{"word":"in-store","surface":"In-store","meaning":"店頭の","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"inflation","surface":"inflation","meaning":"インフレ・物価上昇","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"step up","surface":"stepped up","meaning":"上がる・強まる","pos":"句動詞"},{"word":"year on year","surface":"year on year","meaning":"前年同期比で","pos":"副詞句"}],"grammar":"year on year は経済ニュースの定型。前年の同じ月と比べた変化率を指し、YoY と略される。前月比なら month on month。"},{"id":4,"original":"The increase was led by prices for tinned and packaged food, which increased by 2.5% against 1.1% in the prior month.","translation":"この上昇を主導したのは缶詰やパッケージ食品の価格で、前月の1.1%に対し2.5%上昇した。","words":[{"word":"led by","surface":"led by","meaning":"〜が主導して","pos":"分詞句"},{"word":"tinned","surface":"tinned","meaning":"缶詰の","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"prior","surface":"prior","meaning":"前の・先の","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"which increased by 2.5% は非制限用法の関係代名詞節。コンマの前の内容に補足を加える形で、訳すときは前から順に流すとよい。"},{"id":5,"original":"Food inflation has proved stubborn, squeezing household budgets already stretched by energy bills.","translation":"食品インフレは根強いことが分かってきており、すでに光熱費で逼迫している家計をさらに圧迫している。","words":[{"word":"prove","surface":"proved","meaning":"〜だと分かる","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"stubborn","surface":"stubborn","meaning":"しつこい・根強い","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"squeeze","surface":"squeezing","meaning":"圧迫する・締め付ける","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"household budget","surface":"household budgets","meaning":"家計","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"stretched","surface":"stretched","meaning":"（資金が）逼迫した","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"squeezing 以下は分詞構文。主節の内容がもたらす結果を表し、「〜し、その結果…している」と訳すと自然になる。"},{"id":6,"original":"Meanwhile, Shein's Hong Kong listing on Tuesday comes after a years-long quest to sell shares in New York and London.","translation":"一方、シーインの火曜日の香港上場は、ニューヨークとロンドンでの株式売却を何年も模索した末のものである。","words":[{"word":"listing","surface":"listing","meaning":"上場","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"years-long","surface":"years-long","meaning":"何年にもわたる","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"quest","surface":"quest","meaning":"探求・模索","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"share","surface":"shares","meaning":"株式","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"comes after ... は「〜を経ての出来事だ」。ニュースでは現在形 comes を使って、出来事の背景を示すことが多い。"},{"id":7,"original":"The fast-fashion giant's shares fell in its long-awaited stock market debut.","translation":"ファストファッション大手の株価は、待望の株式市場デビューで下落した。","words":[{"word":"fast-fashion","surface":"fast-fashion","meaning":"ファストファッションの","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"giant","surface":"giant","meaning":"大手企業・巨人","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"long-awaited","surface":"long-awaited","meaning":"待望の","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"debut","surface":"debut","meaning":"デビュー・初登場","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"giant は「巨人」から転じて、業界の最大手企業を指す。tech giant（IT大手）、retail giant（小売大手）のように使う。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"en","country":"イギリス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"en-2026-W36-culture","section":"culture","kind":"blog","title":"Freddie Mercury at 80: the friend who kept the trunks","titleJa":"フレディ・マーキュリー生誕80年 ― トランクを守り続けた友人","leadJa":"今週はフレディ・マーキュリーが80歳を迎えるはずだった週でした。ガーディアン紙は、彼が全財産を託した女性メアリー・オースティンの証言を伝えています。その記事をきっかけに、この特異な関係を本誌が書き下ろします。","category":"文化","level":"上級","trivia":"フレディはメアリーに、ロンドンの邸宅ガーデン・ロッジと楽曲の印税の半分を遺しました。「僕の唯一の友人だった」という言葉とともに。彼女は今もその家に住んでいます。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"This week Freddie Mercury would have turned eighty, and Britain has spent it looking backwards.","translation":"今週、フレディ・マーキュリーは80歳になっているはずだった。そしてイギリスはこの一週間を、振り返ることに費やした。","words":[{"word":"would have turned","surface":"would have turned","meaning":"〜歳になっていたはずだ","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"look backwards","surface":"looking backwards","meaning":"past を振り返る","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"would have + 過去分詞は、実際には起きなかったことを述べる仮定法過去完了。故人の年齢を語るときの定型表現。"},{"id":2,"original":"He was Queen's flamboyant frontman; she was his shy girlfriend, dreaming of marriage.","translation":"彼はクイーンの華やかなフロントマンであり、彼女は結婚を夢見る内気な恋人だった。","words":[{"word":"flamboyant","surface":"flamboyant","meaning":"華やかな・派手な","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"frontman","surface":"frontman","meaning":"フロントマン・バンドの顔","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"shy","surface":"shy","meaning":"内気な","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"セミコロンは、関係の深い二つの文を等しい重みで並べるときに使う。ここでは二人の対比を際立たせている。"},{"id":3,"original":"Then they both realised he preferred men, and the romance ended without the friendship ever doing so.","translation":"やがて二人は、彼が男性を好むことに気づいた。恋は終わったが、友情はついに終わることがなかった。","words":[{"word":"realise","surface":"realised","meaning":"気づく","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"prefer","surface":"preferred","meaning":"〜のほうを好む","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"romance","surface":"romance","meaning":"恋愛関係","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"without the friendship ever doing so の do so は前の ended を受ける代動詞。同じ語の繰り返しを避ける英語らしい技法。"},{"id":4,"original":"Thirty-five years after his death, Mary Austin has begun to talk about their unbreakable bond.","translation":"彼の死から35年、メアリー・オースティンは二人の壊れることのない絆について語り始めた。","words":[{"word":"unbreakable","surface":"unbreakable","meaning":"壊れない","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"bond","surface":"bond","meaning":"絆","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"接頭辞 un- と接尾辞 -able の組み合わせで「〜されえない」。unthinkable、unmistakable なども同じ作りをしている。"},{"id":5,"original":"There were four silver trunks in her attic, packed in the mid-1980s and left unopened for decades.","translation":"彼女の屋根裏には銀色のトランクが四つあった。1980年代半ばに詰められ、何十年も開けられないままだった。","words":[{"word":"trunk","surface":"trunks","meaning":"大型のトランク","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"attic","surface":"attic","meaning":"屋根裏","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"unopened","surface":"unopened","meaning":"開けられていない","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"decade","surface":"decades","meaning":"10年間","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"packed ... and left ... はどちらも trunks を修飾する過去分詞句。名詞のあとに続けて説明を足す、簡潔な書き方。"},{"id":6,"original":"It was too painful. When she finally opened one, it was crammed with lyrics in his handwriting.","translation":"つらすぎたのだ。ようやく一つを開けたとき、そこには彼の筆跡の歌詞がぎっしり詰まっていた。","words":[{"word":"painful","surface":"painful","meaning":"つらい・苦痛な","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"cram","surface":"crammed","meaning":"詰め込む","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"lyrics","surface":"lyrics","meaning":"歌詞","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"handwriting","surface":"handwriting","meaning":"筆跡・手書き","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"be crammed with は「〜でぎっしり詰まっている」。be filled with より密度と乱雑さを感じさせる語感を持つ。"},{"id":7,"original":"Among them were the words to Don't Stop Me Now and Killer Queen, scribbled and crossed out.","translation":"その中には『Don't Stop Me Now』や『Killer Queen』の歌詞が、走り書きされ、消され線を引かれた状態であった。","words":[{"word":"scribble","surface":"scribbled","meaning":"走り書きする","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"cross out","surface":"crossed out","meaning":"線を引いて消す","pos":"句動詞"}],"grammar":"Among them were ... は場所を表す語句を文頭に置いた倒置。主語 the words が動詞 were のあとに来ている。"},{"id":8,"original":"He left her his London house and half of his songwriting royalties, calling her his only true friend.","translation":"彼は彼女にロンドンの家と作曲印税の半分を遺し、彼女を唯一の本当の友人と呼んだ。","words":[{"word":"leave","surface":"left","meaning":"遺す・残す","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"royalty","surface":"royalties","meaning":"印税","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"only","surface":"only","meaning":"唯一の","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"left her his London house は第4文型（SVOO）。leave A B で「AにBを遺す」。calling 以下は付帯状況の分詞構文。"},{"id":9,"original":"She still lives there. Forty years on, she is the one still keeping his things safe.","translation":"彼女は今もそこに暮らしている。40年を経て、彼の遺したものを守り続けているのは彼女なのだ。","words":[{"word":"still","surface":"still","meaning":"今もなお","pos":"副詞"},{"word":"keep safe","surface":"keeping his things safe","meaning":"無事に保つ","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"she is the one who ... の形（ここでは who が省略され現在分詞 keeping が続く）で、「ほかならぬ彼女が〜している」と強調している。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"en","country":"イギリス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"en-2026-W36-life-column","section":"life-column","kind":"blog","title":"Why Britain names its storms","titleJa":"なぜイギリスは嵐に名前を付けるのか","leadJa":"9月1日、イギリスの嵐シーズンが始まりました。オースティン、クロエ、エヴリン ―気象庁が毎年発表する嵐の名前は、単なる遊びではありません。天気の話が国民的な趣味であるこの国ならではの、実用的な理由があります。","category":"生活","level":"中級","trivia":"名前の候補は一般公募で集められます。「自分の名前の嵐に襲われた」という奇妙な経験をした人が、毎年イギリスのどこかに必ずいることになります。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"Every September, the Met Office publishes a list of names, in alphabetical order, that will be given to the storms of the coming winter.","translation":"毎年9月、イギリス気象庁は、来たる冬の嵐に付けられる名前をアルファベット順に並べたリストを発表する。","words":[{"word":"Met Office","surface":"Met Office","meaning":"イギリス気象庁","pos":"固有名詞"},{"word":"publish","surface":"publishes","meaning":"公表する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"in alphabetical order","surface":"in alphabetical order","meaning":"アルファベット順に","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"coming","surface":"coming","meaning":"来たる・次の","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"that will be given to ... は names を修飾する関係詞節。長い挿入句（in alphabetical order）を挟んでも、先行詞は names のまま。"},{"id":2,"original":"To an outsider this looks like a quaint national hobby, filed alongside queuing and talking about the weather.","translation":"外国人の目には、これは行列や天気の話と並ぶ、風変わりな国民的趣味に見えるかもしれない。","words":[{"word":"outsider","surface":"outsider","meaning":"部外者・よそ者","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"quaint","surface":"quaint","meaning":"風変わりで趣のある","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"file","surface":"filed","meaning":"分類する・しまい込む","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"queue","surface":"queuing","meaning":"行列に並ぶ","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"filed alongside ... は過去分詞の分詞構文。「〜と並べて分類された（もののように）」と、前の名詞句に説明を足している。"},{"id":3,"original":"It is nothing of the sort. The naming scheme began in 2015 for an entirely practical reason.","translation":"それはまったく違う。この命名制度は2015年に、きわめて実務的な理由から始まった。","words":[{"word":"nothing of the sort","surface":"nothing of the sort","meaning":"そんなことは全然ない","pos":"名詞句"},{"word":"scheme","surface":"scheme","meaning":"制度・計画","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"entirely","surface":"entirely","meaning":"まったく","pos":"副詞"}],"grammar":"nothing of the sort は前の内容を強く否定する決まり文句。イギリス英語ではやや改まった、書き言葉寄りの響きを持つ。"},{"id":4,"original":"Forecasters had found that warnings about \"an area of low pressure\" simply did not stick in people's minds.","translation":"予報士たちは、「低気圧域」についての警報が人々の記憶にまるで残らないことに気づいていた。","words":[{"word":"forecaster","surface":"Forecasters","meaning":"予報士","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"warning","surface":"warnings","meaning":"警報","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"low pressure","surface":"low pressure","meaning":"低気圧","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"stick","surface":"stick","meaning":"（記憶に）残る","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"had found は過去完了。主節の過去（began）よりさらに前に起きたことを示し、時間の前後関係をはっきりさせている。"},{"id":5,"original":"Give the same weather system a human name, however, and people talk about it, share it, and take it seriously.","translation":"ところが同じ気象システムに人間の名前を付けてやると、人々はそれを話題にし、共有し、真剣に受け止める。","words":[{"word":"weather system","surface":"weather system","meaning":"気象システム・気圧配置","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"however","surface":"however","meaning":"しかしながら","pos":"副詞"},{"word":"take seriously","surface":"take it seriously","meaning":"真剣に受け止める","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"命令法 + and で「〜すれば…する」という条件を表す。If you give ... と同じ意味だが、より簡潔で力強い。"},{"id":6,"original":"There is a strict rule: a storm only gets a name if it is expected to cause enough damage to warrant a warning.","translation":"厳格な規則がある。嵐に名前が付くのは、警報を出すに足る被害が予想される場合に限られる。","words":[{"word":"strict","surface":"strict","meaning":"厳格な","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"expect","surface":"expected","meaning":"予期する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"damage","surface":"damage","meaning":"被害","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"warrant","surface":"warrant","meaning":"〜に値する・正当化する","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"コロンのあとで規則の中身を説明する構成。only ... if ~ で「〜の場合に限って…する」という限定条件を表している。"},{"id":7,"original":"So a named storm is not a joke. It is a signal that someone, somewhere, should be moving the garden furniture indoors.","translation":"だから名前の付いた嵐は冗談ではない。どこかの誰かが庭の家具を屋内にしまうべきだという合図なのだ。","words":[{"word":"signal","surface":"signal","meaning":"合図・信号","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"garden furniture","surface":"garden furniture","meaning":"庭用の家具","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"indoors","surface":"indoors","meaning":"屋内へ","pos":"副詞"}],"grammar":"someone, somewhere とコンマで区切って並べることで「どこかの誰かが」と漠然とした対象を印象づけている。"},{"id":8,"original":"The names themselves are gathered from public suggestions, which is how Britain ends up with storms called Bert and Gerrit.","translation":"名前そのものは一般からの応募で集められる。だからイギリスにはバートやゲリットという名の嵐が生まれることになる。","words":[{"word":"gather","surface":"gathered","meaning":"集める","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"suggestion","surface":"suggestions","meaning":"提案・応募","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"end up with","surface":"ends up with","meaning":"結局〜になる","pos":"句動詞"}],"grammar":"which is how ... は前の文全体を受ける関係代名詞 which。「そういうわけで〜なのだ」と、理由と結果をつなぐ働きをする。"},{"id":9,"original":"This year's list starts with Austen. Come January, half the country will be blaming him for a fallen fence.","translation":"今年のリストはオースティンから始まる。1月ともなれば、国じゅうの半分が倒れたフェンスを彼のせいにしているだろう。","words":[{"word":"come","surface":"Come","meaning":"〜になれば","pos":"前置詞"},{"word":"blame","surface":"blaming","meaning":"〜のせいにする","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"fallen","surface":"fallen","meaning":"倒れた","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"Come January は「1月が来れば」を表す古風で慣用的な用法。Come Monday, come summer のように時を表す語の前に置く。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"en","country":"イギリス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"en-2026-W36-news-brief","section":"news-brief","kind":"news","title":"In brief: storm names, sewage, and a tearful goodbye","titleJa":"今週の短信 ― 嵐の名前、下水、そして涙の別れ","leadJa":"イギリスの今週から三本。嵐に名前を付ける気象庁の恒例行事、水道会社の違法放流をめぐる調査報道、そしてジョコビッチの涙。見出しの英語のリズムに慣れる練習にどうぞ。","source":"BBC News ほか","sourceUrl":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/weather/articles/cn0n01vrw9vo","sources":[{"name":"BBC Weather","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/weather/articles/cn0n01vrw9vo"},{"name":"The Guardian (Business)","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/01/dry-weather-sewage-discharges-soar-as-water-companies-fa"},{"name":"BBC Sport","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/tennis/articles/ckgvrdz061eo"}],"category":"社会","level":"中級","trivia":"イギリスの嵐にはアルファベット順に人名が付きます。名前が付くのは「被害が予想される嵐」だけ。住民が warning を真剣に受け止めるようにという、2015年に始まった仕組みです。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"Tuesday 1 September marks the start of the UK storm season and a new list of storm names have been released.","translation":"9月1日火曜日はイギリスの嵐シーズンの始まりにあたり、新しい嵐の名前のリストが公表された。","words":[{"word":"mark","surface":"marks","meaning":"（節目を）示す","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"storm season","surface":"storm season","meaning":"嵐の季節","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"release","surface":"released","meaning":"公表する","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"mark the start of ... は「〜の幕開けとなる」。日付や出来事を主語にして節目を表す、ニュースの定型表現。"},{"id":2,"original":"The names include Austen, Chloe and Evelyn.","translation":"名前にはオースティン、クロエ、エヴリンなどが含まれる。","words":[{"word":"include","surface":"include","meaning":"含む","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":""},{"id":3,"original":"The number of suspected illegal discharges of raw sewage into rivers and seas by water companies during dry weather increased significantly.","translation":"水道会社が乾燥した天候時に川や海へ未処理下水を違法に放流したと疑われる件数が、大幅に増加した。","words":[{"word":"suspected","surface":"suspected","meaning":"〜の疑いのある","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"discharge","surface":"discharges","meaning":"放流・排出","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"raw sewage","surface":"raw sewage","meaning":"未処理の下水","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"significantly","surface":"significantly","meaning":"大幅に","pos":"副詞"}],"grammar":"The number of ... increased と、主語が長く伸びてから動詞が来る英語らしい構造。どこまでが主語かを見極めるのが読解の鍵。"},{"id":4,"original":"Dumping raw sewage into waterways during dry spells amounts to pollution, and it is considered a breach of the permits given to water companies.","translation":"乾燥期に未処理下水を水路へ投棄することは汚染にあたり、水道会社に与えられた許可の違反とみなされる。","words":[{"word":"dump","surface":"Dumping","meaning":"投棄する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"dry spell","surface":"dry spells","meaning":"乾燥した時期","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"amount to","surface":"amounts to","meaning":"〜に相当する","pos":"句動詞"},{"word":"breach","surface":"breach","meaning":"違反","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"permit","surface":"permits","meaning":"許可・認可","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"文頭の Dumping は動名詞で主語。「〜すること」を主語に立てる形で、フォーマルな英語で頻繁に使われる。"},{"id":5,"original":"After Novak Djokovic's latest bid for a historic 25th major title ends in tears in New York, where does the most decorated men's player of the Open era go from here?","translation":"歴史的なメジャー25勝目を目指したノバク・ジョコビッチの最新の挑戦がニューヨークで涙に終わった今、オープン化以降で最も多くの栄冠を手にした男子選手はどこへ向かうのか。","words":[{"word":"bid","surface":"bid","meaning":"挑戦・試み","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"end in tears","surface":"ends in tears","meaning":"涙に終わる","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"decorated","surface":"decorated","meaning":"栄誉に輝いた","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"era","surface":"era","meaning":"時代","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"where does ... go from here? は「ここからどこへ向かうのか」＝今後どうするのか、を問う決まった言い方。記事の締めによく置かれる。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"en","country":"イギリス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"en-2026-W36-street-talk","section":"street-talk","kind":"dialogue","title":"\"Have you seen the price of a tin of beans?\"","titleJa":"「豆の缶詰の値段、見た？」― パブでの15分","leadJa":"金曜の夕方、マンチェスターのパブ。デイヴとプリヤが物価の話を始めます。イギリス英語の口語表現がぎっしり ― quid、blimey、mind you、fair enough。教科書には出てこないけれど、現地では毎日聞こえてくる言い回しです。","category":"生活","level":"中級","trivia":"quid は「ポンド」の俗称で、複数形も quid のまま（five quid）。同じくイギリスでは「10ポンド札」を a tenner、「5ポンド札」を a fiver と呼びます。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"Right, what are you having? My round.","speaker":"Dave","translation":"さて、何にする？俺のおごりだよ。","words":[{"word":"Right","surface":"Right","meaning":"さて・よし","pos":"間投詞"},{"word":"round","surface":"round","meaning":"（酒の）一巡・おごりの番","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"My round. は「今回は自分が全員分おごる番だ」という意味。イギリスのパブ文化では、順番におごり合う round が慣習になっている。"},{"id":2,"original":"Just a lime and soda for me, ta. I'm driving.","speaker":"Priya","translation":"ライムソーダだけでいいわ、ありがと。運転あるから。","words":[{"word":"ta","surface":"ta","meaning":"ありがと（thank you のくだけた形）","pos":"間投詞"}],"grammar":"ta は北イングランドを中心に広く使われる、ごく軽い「ありがとう」。友人同士や店先で使い、目上には使わない。"},{"id":3,"original":"Fair enough. Blimey, four quid for a soft drink now.","speaker":"Dave","translation":"了解。うわ、ソフトドリンクが今や4ポンドかよ。","words":[{"word":"Fair enough","surface":"Fair enough","meaning":"なるほど・了解","pos":"決まり文句"},{"word":"Blimey","surface":"Blimey","meaning":"うわ・なんてこった","pos":"間投詞"},{"word":"quid","surface":"quid","meaning":"ポンド（口語）","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Fair enough は相手の言い分を受け入れるときの相槌。「まあそれなら仕方ない」「了解」と、納得を示す万能表現。"},{"id":4,"original":"Tell me about it. Have you seen the price of a tin of beans?","speaker":"Priya","translation":"ほんとよね。豆の缶詰の値段、見た？","words":[{"word":"Tell me about it","surface":"Tell me about it","meaning":"ほんとにそうだよね","pos":"決まり文句"},{"word":"tin","surface":"tin","meaning":"缶","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Tell me about it. は文字通りなら「それについて話して」だが、実際には「まったくその通り」と強い共感を表す皮肉めいた相槌。"},{"id":5,"original":"Went up again, didn't it. The shop prices are the worst they've been in two years, apparently.","speaker":"Dave","translation":"また上がったよな。店頭価格はここ2年で一番ひどいらしいよ。","words":[{"word":"go up","surface":"Went up","meaning":"上がる","pos":"句動詞"},{"word":"apparently","surface":"apparently","meaning":"どうやら・〜らしい","pos":"副詞"}],"grammar":"Went up again, didn't it. は主語 It が省略された話し言葉。付加疑問 didn't it が下がり調子だと、同意を求めるというより独り言に近い。"},{"id":6,"original":"It's the energy bills doing it, mostly. Everything that gets cooked or chilled costs more.","speaker":"Priya","translation":"だいたいは光熱費のせいよ。調理も冷蔵も、通すものは全部高くなる。","words":[{"word":"energy bill","surface":"energy bills","meaning":"光熱費","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"chill","surface":"chilled","meaning":"冷やす・冷蔵する","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"It's the energy bills doing it は強調構文 It is ... that ... の口語版。that を省き、doing it と続けて「〜のせいだ」と原因を指す。"},{"id":7,"original":"Mind you, my nan reckons it was worse in the seventies.","speaker":"Dave","translation":"とはいえ、うちのばあちゃんは70年代のほうがひどかったって言うけどな。","words":[{"word":"Mind you","surface":"Mind you","meaning":"とはいえ・ただし","pos":"決まり文句"},{"word":"nan","surface":"nan","meaning":"おばあちゃん","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"reckon","surface":"reckons","meaning":"〜だと思う","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"Mind you は自分の直前の発言に条件や留保を付け足すときのつなぎ。「もっとも」「そうは言っても」に近い。"},{"id":8,"original":"She's not wrong. Inflation hit twenty-odd per cent back then.","speaker":"Priya","translation":"間違ってないわね。あのころインフレは20%台に達したんだから。","words":[{"word":"odd","surface":"-odd","meaning":"〜あまり・〜すこし","pos":"接尾辞"},{"word":"hit","surface":"hit","meaning":"（数値に）達する","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"She's not wrong. は「その通りだ」を控えめに言う言い方。イギリス英語では、直接的な同意を避けた婉曲表現が好まれる。"},{"id":9,"original":"Suppose. Doesn't help much when you're at the till, though, does it.","speaker":"Dave","translation":"だろうね。でもレジに立ってるときには何の慰めにもならないけどな。","words":[{"word":"Suppose","surface":"Suppose","meaning":"だろうね（I suppose の省略）","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"till","surface":"till","meaning":"レジ","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Doesn't help much ... does it. も主語 It の省略。イギリスの話し言葉では、文頭の主語や助動詞がしばしば落ちる。"},{"id":10,"original":"No. Anyway, storm season starts today. That's cheered me right up.","speaker":"Priya","translation":"ならないわね。ところで今日から嵐のシーズンよ。おかげですっかり元気が出たわ。","words":[{"word":"Anyway","surface":"Anyway","meaning":"ところで・それはさておき","pos":"副詞"},{"word":"cheer up","surface":"cheered me right up","meaning":"元気づける","pos":"句動詞"}],"grammar":"right は「すっかり・完全に」という強調の副詞。cheered me right up、turn right around のように動詞句を強める口語用法。"},{"id":11,"original":"Ha! What have they called them this year?","speaker":"Dave","translation":"はは！今年は何て名前を付けたんだ？","words":[{"word":"call","surface":"called","meaning":"〜と名づける","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"call them + 名前 は第5文型（SVOC）。「them を〜と呼ぶ」で、名前を尋ねるときの自然な言い方。"},{"id":12,"original":"Austen, Chloe, Evelyn. Sounds like a law firm, not a load of gales.","speaker":"Priya","translation":"オースティン、クロエ、エヴリン。強風の一群っていうより法律事務所みたいね。","words":[{"word":"law firm","surface":"law firm","meaning":"法律事務所","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"a load of","surface":"a load of","meaning":"たくさんの","pos":"限定詞句"},{"word":"gale","surface":"gales","meaning":"強風","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Sounds like ... も主語 It の省略。a load of は口語で「たくさんの」、文脈によっては軽い侮蔑（a load of rubbish）にもなる。"},{"id":13,"original":"Storm Evelyn ruining my fence in November. Can picture it now.","speaker":"Dave","translation":"11月にエヴリン嵐がうちのフェンスを壊すわけだ。もう目に浮かぶよ。","words":[{"word":"ruin","surface":"ruining","meaning":"台無しにする","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"fence","surface":"fence","meaning":"フェンス・垣根","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"picture","surface":"picture","meaning":"思い描く","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"Can picture it now. は I が落ちた形。picture は動詞で「頭に思い描く」の意味になり、I can picture it. で「目に浮かぶ」。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"fr","country":"フランス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"fr-2026-W36-buzzword","section":"buzzword","kind":"buzzword","title":"Les mots de la semaine","titleJa":"今週のことば ― 新学期のフランス語5語","leadJa":"今週フランスのニュースと会話に何度も登場した5語。辞書の訳語だけでは届かない、いま使われている感覚まで押さえておきましょう。","category":"語彙","level":"中級","trivia":"rentrée は動詞 rentrer（戻る）の女性名詞形。同じように sortie（外出・発売）、entrée（入口・前菜）も動詞から生まれた名詞です。"},"entries":[{"term":"la rentrée","reading":"","meaning":"新学期・新年度の始まり","note":"9月にフランス全体が動き出す時期そのものを指す。学校だけでなく、政界の rentrée politique、出版界の rentrée littéraire にも使う。「休み明けの仕切り直し」という国民的な気分を含んだ語。","example":"Bonne rentrée à tous les élèves !","exampleJa":"生徒のみなさん、よい新学期を！"},{"term":"le portable","reading":"","meaning":"携帯電話・スマートフォン","note":"téléphone portable の略で、日常会話ではこちらが普通。同じ意味で mobile も使うが、フランス本国では portable が優勢。ノートPCは ordinateur portable。","example":"Éteins ton portable, on est à table.","exampleJa":"携帯を切りなさい、食事中でしょう。"},{"term":"en cachette","reading":"","meaning":"こっそり・隠れて","note":"cachette（隠れ場所）から。今週は「スマホ禁止でもどうせ en cachette で使う」という生徒たちの反応として各紙に登場した。en secret より日常的で、いたずらっぽい響きがある。","example":"Il fume en cachette depuis des années.","exampleJa":"彼は何年も前から隠れてたばこを吸っている。"},{"term":"entrer en vigueur","reading":"","meaning":"施行される・発効する","note":"法律や規則が効力を持ち始めること。ニュースの定型表現だが、新しい校則や社内ルールの話でも普通に使われる。主語は必ず規則や法律の側。","example":"La nouvelle règle entre en vigueur dès lundi.","exampleJa":"新しい規則は月曜から施行される。"},{"term":"du coup","reading":"","meaning":"だから・それで・つまり","note":"現代フランス語で最も多用される口語のつなぎ言葉。本来は「その結果」だが、いまでは意味がかなり薄れ、話の区切りごとに挟まれる。多用しすぎると若者っぽく響く。","example":"J'ai raté mon train, du coup je serai en retard.","exampleJa":"電車に乗り遅れた。だから遅刻する。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"fr","country":"フランス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"fr-2026-W36-cover-story","section":"cover-story","kind":"news","title":"La rentrée 2026 : 11,6 millions d'élèves et un lycée sans portable","titleJa":"2026年の新学期 ― 1160万人が登校、高校はスマホ禁止に","leadJa":"9月1日、フランスは一年で最も国民的な日のひとつ「ラ・ラントレ」を迎えました。今年の目玉は高校での携帯電話の全面禁止。生徒たちの反応は冷ややかで、制服の試験導入は静かに幕を閉じました。フランス各紙の配信記事から今週の教室をのぞきます。","source":"France 24 ほか","sourceUrl":"https://www.france24.com/fr/vidéo/20260901-rentrée-scolaire-entrée-en-vigueur-de-l-interdiction-du-portable-au-lycée","sources":[{"name":"France 24","url":"https://www.france24.com/fr/vidéo/20260901-rentrée-scolaire-entrée-en-vigueur-de-l-interdiction-du-portable-au-lycée"},{"name":"Le Figaro","url":"https://etudiant.lefigaro.fr/article/lycee/rentree-scolaire-2026-interdiction-du-portable-au-lycee-questionnai"},{"name":"Le Figaro (Lyon)","url":"https://www.lefigaro.fr/lyon/rentree-scolaire-a-lyon-des-brasseurs-d-air-dans-les-classes-mais-pas-de-climatis"},{"name":"RFI","url":"https://www.rfi.fr/fr/france/20260901-uniforme-à-l-école-en-france-la-fin-discrète-d-une-expérimentation-qui-n-a-pas-convaincu"}],"category":"社会","level":"中級","trivia":"「ラ・ラントレ」は学校だけの言葉ではありません。バカンス明けに国全体が動き出す9月を指し、政界の再始動は rentrée politique、出版界の新刊ラッシュは rentrée littéraire と呼ばれます。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"Quelque 11,6 millions d'écoliers, collégiens et lycéens font mardi leur rentrée, marquée par quelques nouveautés, comme l'interdiction du portable au lycée, et pour certains par des perturbations après une importante cyberattaque ayant visé l'Éducation nationale.","translation":"約1160万人の小学生・中学生・高校生が火曜日に新学期を迎える。高校での携帯電話禁止といった新制度が目を引くほか、一部では国民教育省を狙った大規模なサイバー攻撃による混乱も出ている。","words":[{"word":"écolier","surface":"écoliers","meaning":"小学生","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"collégien","surface":"collégiens","meaning":"中学生","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"lycéen","surface":"lycéens","meaning":"高校生","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"rentrée","surface":"rentrée","meaning":"新学期・新年度の始まり","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"interdiction","surface":"interdiction","meaning":"禁止","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"perturbation","surface":"perturbations","meaning":"混乱・乱れ","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"文末の ayant visé は現在分詞の複合形。直前の cyberattaque を後ろから修飾し、「（すでに）〜を狙った」と完了した動作を表す。"},{"id":2,"original":"C'est la rentrée pour près de 12 millions de jeunes Français ce mardi 1er septembre.","translation":"9月1日火曜日、約1200万人のフランスの若者にとって新学期が始まる。","words":[{"word":"près de","surface":"près de","meaning":"およそ・約","pos":"前置詞句"},{"word":"jeune","surface":"jeunes","meaning":"若者","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"près de + 数詞で「およそ〜」。数量表現の de のあとには冠詞を置かない（de 12 millions de jeunes）。"},{"id":3,"original":"Après les collégiens, les lycéens devront se passer de leur téléphone portable au lycée dès la rentrée.","translation":"中学生に続き、高校生も新学期から校内では携帯電話なしで過ごさなければならなくなる。","words":[{"word":"se passer de","surface":"se passer de","meaning":"〜なしで済ませる","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"portable","surface":"portable","meaning":"携帯電話","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"dès","surface":"dès","meaning":"〜から早くも","pos":"前置詞"}],"grammar":"devront は devoir の単純未来。se passer de は代名動詞で「〜なしで済ませる」。同じ passer でも se passer だけだと「起こる」の意味になる。"},{"id":4,"original":"En ce jour de rentrée, les élèves devront se séparer de leur téléphone avant d'entrer en classe.","translation":"新学期のこの日、生徒たちは教室に入る前に携帯電話を手放さなければならない。","words":[{"word":"se séparer de","surface":"se séparer de","meaning":"〜を手放す・〜と別れる","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"élève","surface":"élèves","meaning":"生徒","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"avant de + 不定詞で「〜する前に」。主節と主語が同じときはこの形を使い、主語が違うときは avant que + 接続法になる。"},{"id":5,"original":"Mais la mesure d'interdiction des réseaux sociaux aux moins de 15 ans n'a, elle, pas abouti pour l'heure.","translation":"一方、15歳未満へのSNS禁止措置のほうは、今のところ実現していない。","words":[{"word":"mesure","surface":"mesure","meaning":"措置・対策","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"réseaux sociaux","surface":"réseaux sociaux","meaning":"SNS・ソーシャルメディア","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"aboutir","surface":"abouti","meaning":"実を結ぶ・成立する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"pour l'heure","surface":"pour l'heure","meaning":"今のところ","pos":"副詞句"}],"grammar":"n'a, elle, pas abouti は ne...pas の間に強勢代名詞 elle を挟んだ書き言葉的な語順。「（他はともかく）この措置のほうは」と主語を際立たせる。"},{"id":6,"original":"Au terme d'un été caniculaire, les élèves lyonnais s'apprêtent à reprendre le chemin d'écoles encore peu adaptées aux chaleurs extrêmes.","translation":"猛暑の夏が明け、リヨンの生徒たちは、極端な暑さにいまだほとんど対応できていない校舎へ再び通い始めようとしている。","words":[{"word":"au terme de","surface":"Au terme d'","meaning":"〜の終わりに","pos":"前置詞句"},{"word":"caniculaire","surface":"caniculaire","meaning":"猛暑の","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"s'apprêter à","surface":"s'apprêtent à","meaning":"まさに〜しようとしている","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"reprendre le chemin de","surface":"reprendre le chemin d'","meaning":"〜へまた通い出す","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"peu adaptées の peu は「ほとんど〜ない」という否定的な程度を表す。un peu（少し）とは意味が逆になるので注意。"},{"id":7,"original":"L'expérimentation de la tenue scolaire commune ne sera pas reconduite à la rentrée 2026.","translation":"共通制服の試験導入は、2026年の新学期には継続されない。","words":[{"word":"expérimentation","surface":"expérimentation","meaning":"試験的導入","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"tenue scolaire","surface":"tenue scolaire","meaning":"制服・学校の服装","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"reconduire","surface":"reconduite","meaning":"更新する・継続する","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"ne sera pas reconduite は単純未来の受動態。主語 expérimentation が女性単数なので、過去分詞が reconduite と性数一致している。"},{"id":8,"original":"Lancé en 2024, le dispositif devait notamment renforcer la cohésion entre élèves et améliorer le climat scolaire.","translation":"2024年に始まったこの制度は、生徒どうしの結束を強め、学校の雰囲気を改善することを主な狙いとしていた。","words":[{"word":"dispositif","surface":"dispositif","meaning":"制度・仕組み","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"renforcer","surface":"renforcer","meaning":"強化する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"cohésion","surface":"cohésion","meaning":"結束・まとまり","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"climat scolaire","surface":"climat scolaire","meaning":"学校の雰囲気・風土","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"文頭の Lancé en 2024 は過去分詞による分詞構文。あとに続く le dispositif を修飾し「2024年に始められたこの制度は」の意味になる。"},{"id":9,"original":"Deux ans plus tard, le bilan officiel est contrasté : les élèves interrogés par des chercheurs rejettent massivement le principe et les collectivités ne disposent plus du même soutien financier de l'État.","translation":"2年後、公式の総括は評価が分かれるものとなった。研究者の調査に答えた生徒たちは制度そのものを大きく拒み、自治体も国から以前と同じ財政支援を受けられなくなっている。","words":[{"word":"bilan","surface":"bilan","meaning":"総括・収支決算","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"contrasté","surface":"contrasté","meaning":"評価が分かれる・まちまちの","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"rejeter","surface":"rejettent","meaning":"拒む・退ける","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"collectivité","surface":"collectivités","meaning":"自治体","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"disposer de","surface":"disposent","meaning":"自由に使える・持っている","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"ne...plus で「もう〜ない」。ここでは disposer de の de と定冠詞 le が縮約して du になっている（ne disposent plus du même soutien）。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"fr","country":"フランス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"fr-2026-W36-culture","section":"culture","kind":"blog","title":"La rentrée littéraire : 500 romans en deux mois","titleJa":"ラントレ・リテレール ― 2か月で500冊が並ぶ季節","leadJa":"9月のフランスでは、書店に途方もない数の新刊小説が押し寄せます。秋の文学賞レースへ向けた出版界の一大行事「ラントレ・リテレール」を、書き下ろしのコラムでご案内します。","category":"文化","level":"上級","trivia":"ゴンクール賞の賞金はわずか10ユーロ。しかし受賞すれば数十万部が動くため、出版社にとっては桁違いの価値を持つ、世界でもっとも安くて高い文学賞です。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"Chaque automne, les éditeurs français se livrent à un rituel qui étonne toujours les étrangers.","translation":"毎年秋、フランスの出版社は、外国人をいつも驚かせる恒例行事にいそしむ。","words":[{"word":"éditeur","surface":"éditeurs","meaning":"出版社・編集者","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"se livrer à","surface":"se livrent à","meaning":"（行為に）ふける・打ち込む","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"rituel","surface":"rituel","meaning":"儀式・恒例行事","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"étonner","surface":"étonne","meaning":"驚かせる","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"qui étonne toujours les étrangers は関係代名詞 qui の節で、先行詞 un rituel を説明している。qui は節の中で主語の役割を果たす。"},{"id":2,"original":"Entre la fin août et octobre, près de cinq cents romans paraissent en quelques semaines.","translation":"8月末から10月にかけて、およそ500冊の小説が数週間のうちに刊行される。","words":[{"word":"paraître","surface":"paraissent","meaning":"刊行される・現れる","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"roman","surface":"romans","meaning":"小説","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Entre A et B で期間を表す。cinq cents は複数の s が付くが、後ろに別の数詞が続くと cinq cent trois のように s が消える。"},{"id":3,"original":"C'est ce qu'on appelle la rentrée littéraire, et c'est une bataille commerciale autant qu'un moment culturel.","translation":"これがいわゆる「ラントレ・リテレール」であり、文化的な季節であると同時に商戦でもある。","words":[{"word":"ce qu'on appelle","surface":"ce qu'on appelle","meaning":"いわゆる・〜と呼ばれるもの","pos":"関係詞句"},{"word":"bataille","surface":"bataille","meaning":"戦い・争い","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"autant que","surface":"autant qu'","meaning":"〜と同じくらい","pos":"接続詞句"}],"grammar":"ce que は「〜するもの・こと」を表す関係代名詞。ここでは appeler の目的語にあたり「人々がそう呼ぶもの」の意味になる。"},{"id":4,"original":"Les grands prix d'automne, le Goncourt en tête, décideront lesquels seront lus et lesquels seront oubliés.","translation":"秋の主要な文学賞、なかでもゴンクール賞が、どれが読まれ、どれが忘れられるかを決めることになる。","words":[{"word":"prix","surface":"prix","meaning":"賞","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"en tête","surface":"en tête","meaning":"筆頭に・先頭に","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"décider","surface":"décideront","meaning":"決める","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"oublier","surface":"oubliés","meaning":"忘れる","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"lesquels は疑問代名詞 lequel の男性複数形で、ここでは「どちらの本が」を指す。関係代名詞としても使えるので文脈で見分ける。"},{"id":5,"original":"Les libraires, eux, croulent sous les cartons et doivent choisir ce qu'ils mettront en vitrine.","translation":"一方の書店員は段ボールの山に埋もれ、何をショーウィンドウに並べるかを選ばなければならない。","words":[{"word":"libraire","surface":"libraires","meaning":"書店員","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"crouler sous","surface":"croulent sous","meaning":"〜の重みで押しつぶされる","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"carton","surface":"cartons","meaning":"段ボール箱","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"vitrine","surface":"vitrine","meaning":"ショーウィンドウ","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Les libraires, eux, ... と強勢代名詞 eux を挟むのは「彼らのほうはといえば」という対比の合図。前段の出版社と対置している。"},{"id":6,"original":"Beaucoup de ces livres disparaîtront avant Noël, sans que personne ne s'en souvienne.","translation":"これらの本の多くは、誰の記憶にも残らないままクリスマス前に姿を消すだろう。","words":[{"word":"disparaître","surface":"disparaîtront","meaning":"消える","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"sans que","surface":"sans que","meaning":"〜することなしに","pos":"接続詞句"},{"word":"se souvenir de","surface":"s'en souvienne","meaning":"覚えている","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"sans que のあとは必ず接続法（souvienne）。ここに現れる ne は否定ではなく、文語的な虚辞の ne で訳さない。"},{"id":7,"original":"Mais deux ou trois d'entre eux resteront, et c'est pour eux que tout ce vacarme existe.","translation":"だがそのうちの二、三冊は残る。そしてその数冊のために、この喧噪のすべてがある。","words":[{"word":"d'entre eux","surface":"d'entre eux","meaning":"彼ら（それら）のうちの","pos":"前置詞句"},{"word":"rester","surface":"resteront","meaning":"残る","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"vacarme","surface":"vacarme","meaning":"喧噪・大騒ぎ","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"c'est pour eux que... は強調構文 c'est ... que。「ほかでもないその数冊のために」と、pour eux の部分を際立たせている。"},{"id":8,"original":"Si vous passez à Paris en septembre, entrez dans une librairie un samedi après-midi.","translation":"9月にパリに立ち寄るなら、土曜の午後に書店へ入ってみてほしい。","words":[{"word":"passer à","surface":"passez à","meaning":"立ち寄る","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"librairie","surface":"librairie","meaning":"書店","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Si + 直説法現在, 命令法 という形。「もし〜なら…しなさい」という現実的な条件を表す最も基本的な si の使い方。"},{"id":9,"original":"Vous comprendrez tout de suite que lire, ici, reste une affaire sérieuse.","translation":"読むという行為がこの国では今なお真剣な営みであることが、すぐに分かるはずだ。","words":[{"word":"tout de suite","surface":"tout de suite","meaning":"すぐに","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"rester","surface":"reste","meaning":"〜のままである","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"affaire","surface":"affaire","meaning":"事柄・仕事","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"que lire ... reste の主語は不定詞 lire。フランス語では不定詞をそのまま主語にでき、「読むこと」という意味になる。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"fr","country":"フランス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"fr-2026-W36-life-column","section":"life-column","kind":"blog","title":"Septembre, ou l'art français de tout recommencer","titleJa":"9月、フランス流「やり直し」の作法","leadJa":"フランス人にとって一年の始まりは1月ではなく9月かもしれません。バカンスが終わり、学校も職場も政治も出版も、いっせいに動き出す ― この国民的な「仕切り直し」の感覚を、書き下ろしのコラムで味わってください。","category":"生活","level":"中級","trivia":"9月に売れるのが agenda（手帳）。フランスの手帳は1月始まりではなく9月始まりのものが本屋に平積みされます。学年が9月に始まるからです。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"En France, la vraie nouvelle année ne commence pas en janvier. Elle commence en septembre.","translation":"フランスでは、本当の新年は1月に始まるのではない。9月に始まるのだ。","words":[{"word":"vrai","surface":"vraie","meaning":"本当の","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"commencer","surface":"commence","meaning":"始まる","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"ne commence pas en janvier / Elle commence en septembre と、否定文のあとに肯定文を続けて対比を作る書き方。文章に切れ味が出る。"},{"id":2,"original":"Tout le pays part en vacances au mois d'août, et tout le pays revient en même temps.","translation":"国じゅうが8月に休暇へ出かけ、そして国じゅうが同時に戻ってくる。","words":[{"word":"partir en vacances","surface":"part en vacances","meaning":"休暇に出かける","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"en même temps","surface":"en même temps","meaning":"同時に","pos":"副詞句"}],"grammar":"Tout le pays を主語に繰り返すことでリズムを作っている。tout le pays は単数扱いなので動詞も part / revient と単数形。"},{"id":3,"original":"On appelle ce moment la rentrée, et il n'existe pas vraiment d'équivalent en japonais.","translation":"この時期を「ラ・ラントレ」と呼ぶが、日本語にぴったり当たる言葉はない。","words":[{"word":"appeler","surface":"appelle","meaning":"〜と呼ぶ","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"équivalent","surface":"équivalent","meaning":"同等のもの・対応語","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"il n'existe pas de + 無冠詞名詞で「〜は存在しない」。否定文では不定冠詞 un/une/des が de に変わる規則が働いている。"},{"id":4,"original":"Ce n'est pas seulement la rentrée des classes : il y a aussi la rentrée politique, la rentrée littéraire et même la rentrée sociale.","translation":"それは学校の新学期だけを指すのではない。政界の再始動があり、出版界の新刊シーズンがあり、労働運動の再開まである。","words":[{"word":"ne...pas seulement","surface":"n'est pas seulement","meaning":"〜だけではない","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"rentrée littéraire","surface":"rentrée littéraire","meaning":"文学の新刊シーズン","pos":"名詞句"},{"word":"même","surface":"même","meaning":"〜さえも","pos":"副詞"}],"grammar":"コロン（:）は前文の内容を具体的に言い換えるときに使う。フランス語では英語より頻繁に、説明の合図として登場する。"},{"id":5,"original":"Dans les librairies, des centaines de romans sortent en quelques semaines, et les critiques se disputent pour savoir lequel sera le livre de l'automne.","translation":"書店では数週間のうちに何百もの小説が刊行され、批評家たちはどれが今秋の一冊になるかをめぐって言い争う。","words":[{"word":"librairie","surface":"librairies","meaning":"書店","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"sortir","surface":"sortent","meaning":"発売される","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"se disputer","surface":"se disputent","meaning":"言い争う","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"lequel","surface":"lequel","meaning":"どれが（疑問代名詞）","pos":"代名詞"}],"grammar":"pour savoir lequel sera... は間接疑問。疑問詞 lequel のあとは平叙文の語順のままで、倒置しない。"},{"id":6,"original":"Au bureau, la première question n'est jamais professionnelle : « Tu as passé de bonnes vacances ? »","translation":"職場で最初に交わされる質問は、決して仕事の話ではない。「休暇はよかった？」だ。","words":[{"word":"bureau","surface":"bureau","meaning":"職場・オフィス","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"ne...jamais","surface":"n'est jamais","meaning":"決して〜ない","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"passer de bonnes vacances","surface":"passé de bonnes vacances","meaning":"よい休暇を過ごす","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"de bonnes vacances は des ではなく de。形容詞が複数名詞の前に来ると des が de になるという書き言葉の規則による。"},{"id":7,"original":"Il faut y répondre, sinon on passe pour quelqu'un de froid.","translation":"これには答えなければならない。さもないと、冷たい人だと思われてしまう。","words":[{"word":"il faut","surface":"Il faut","meaning":"〜しなければならない","pos":"非人称動詞"},{"word":"sinon","surface":"sinon","meaning":"さもないと","pos":"接続詞"},{"word":"passer pour","surface":"passe pour","meaning":"〜と見なされる","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"quelqu'un de froid のように、quelqu'un / quelque chose を形容詞で修飾するときは必ず de を挟み、形容詞は男性単数形にする。"},{"id":8,"original":"Puis viennent les inscriptions : judo, piano, poterie, cours de yoga du mardi soir.","translation":"続いて申し込みの季節が来る。柔道、ピアノ、陶芸、火曜夜のヨガ教室。","words":[{"word":"puis","surface":"Puis","meaning":"それから","pos":"副詞"},{"word":"inscription","surface":"inscriptions","meaning":"登録・申し込み","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"poterie","surface":"poterie","meaning":"陶芸","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Puis viennent les inscriptions は主語と動詞の倒置。副詞で文を始めると、書き言葉ではこのように動詞を先に置くことがある。"},{"id":9,"original":"Chaque année, on jure de s'y tenir. Chaque année, on abandonne vers la Toussaint.","translation":"毎年、続けると誓う。そして毎年、諸聖人の日のころには投げ出している。","words":[{"word":"jurer","surface":"jure","meaning":"誓う","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"s'y tenir","surface":"s'y tenir","meaning":"それを守り続ける","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"abandonner","surface":"abandonne","meaning":"やめる・投げ出す","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"Toussaint","surface":"Toussaint","meaning":"諸聖人の日（11月1日）","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Chaque année を二度繰り返し、対になる二文を並べることで皮肉を効かせている。文学的な書き言葉でよく使われる技法。"},{"id":10,"original":"Mais peu importe : en septembre, on a le droit de croire qu'on sera quelqu'un de mieux.","translation":"だがそれはどうでもいい。9月には、自分がもっとましな人間になれると信じる権利があるのだから。","words":[{"word":"peu importe","surface":"peu importe","meaning":"どうでもよい・構わない","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"avoir le droit de","surface":"a le droit de","meaning":"〜する権利がある","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"mieux","surface":"mieux","meaning":"よりよい・ましな","pos":"副詞"}],"grammar":"croire que のあとは直説法（sera）。croire が否定や疑問になると接続法をとることがあるが、肯定文では直説法のまま。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"fr","country":"フランス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"fr-2026-W36-news-brief","section":"news-brief","kind":"news","title":"En bref : Messi, l'Himalaya, le bœuf brésilien","titleJa":"今週の短信 ― メッシ、ヒマラヤ、ブラジル産牛肉","leadJa":"フランスの各紙が今週伝えた三つの話題を、配信要約のまま短く。スポーツ、災害、そしてEUの通商 ― ニュースの文体に慣れる練習にちょうどよい長さです。","source":"France 24","sourceUrl":"https://www.france24.com/fr/","sources":[{"name":"France 24 (Sports)","url":"https://www.france24.com/fr/émissions/sports/20260901-le-monument-argentin-lionel-messi-annonce-sa-retraite-internationale"},{"name":"France 24 (Asie-Pacifique)","url":"https://www.france24.com/fr/asie-pacifique/20260901-crue-dévastatrice-himalaya-nepal-chine-tibet-bilan-dépasse-1000-morts"},{"name":"France 24 (Éco-tech)","url":"https://www.france24.com/fr/éco-tech/20260901-union-europeenne-va-suspendre-importations-viande-bresil-sante-regles-sanitaires-antibiotiques-antimicrobiens"}],"category":"国際","level":"中級","trivia":"フランスのニュースは数字を «11,6» のようにコンマで書きます。小数点がコンマ、桁区切りは空白（1 003）。読み上げるときは virgule（コンマ）と言います。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"À 39 ans, Lionel Messi a annoncé la fin de sa carrière internationale, après 207 matchs avec l'Argentine.","translation":"39歳のリオネル・メッシが、アルゼンチン代表として207試合を戦ったのち、代表引退を発表した。","words":[{"word":"annoncer","surface":"annoncé","meaning":"発表する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"carrière","surface":"carrière","meaning":"経歴・キャリア","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"match","surface":"matchs","meaning":"試合","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"À 39 ans のように「à + 年齢」で「〜歳で」。年齢を文頭に置いて主語の状況を先に示すのはニュース文の定型。"},{"id":2,"original":"Avec 125 buts, il est largement le meilleur buteur de l'histoire de sa sélection.","translation":"125ゴールを挙げ、代表史上の得点王として他を大きく引き離している。","words":[{"word":"but","surface":"buts","meaning":"ゴール・得点","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"largement","surface":"largement","meaning":"大きく・ゆうに","pos":"副詞"},{"word":"buteur","surface":"buteur","meaning":"得点者・ストライカー","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"sélection","surface":"sélection","meaning":"代表チーム","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"le meilleur buteur は bon の最上級。形容詞 bon は比較級 meilleur、最上級 le meilleur と不規則に変化する。"},{"id":3,"original":"La crue dévastatrice survenue mercredi dernier dans l'Himalaya a fait 987 morts au Népal, a annoncé mardi l'autorité népalaise chargée des situations d'urgence.","translation":"先週水曜日にヒマラヤで起きた壊滅的な洪水により、ネパールで987人が死亡したと、同国の緊急事態対応当局が火曜日に発表した。","words":[{"word":"crue","surface":"crue","meaning":"増水・洪水","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"dévastateur","surface":"dévastatrice","meaning":"壊滅的な","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"survenir","surface":"survenue","meaning":"（不意に）起こる","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"faire des morts","surface":"a fait 987 morts","meaning":"死者を出す","pos":"動詞句"},{"word":"chargé de","surface":"chargée des","meaning":"〜を担当する","pos":"形容詞句"}],"grammar":"文末の a annoncé mardi l'autorité... は主語と動詞が入れ替わった倒置。引用元を後ろに置くニュース特有の書き方で、日本語の「〜と当局は発表した」にあたる。"},{"id":4,"original":"Le bilan provisoire de la catastrophe atteint ainsi 1 003 morts en y ajoutant les 16 victimes recensées en Chine.","translation":"中国で確認された16人の犠牲者を加えると、この災害の暫定的な死者数は1003人に達する。","words":[{"word":"bilan","surface":"bilan","meaning":"（被害の）集計・総括","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"provisoire","surface":"provisoire","meaning":"暫定的な","pos":"形容詞"},{"word":"atteindre","surface":"atteint","meaning":"達する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"recenser","surface":"recensées","meaning":"数え上げる・集計する","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"en y ajoutant は「en + 現在分詞」のジェロンディフで手段を表し、y は「そこに＝この集計に」を指す。「それを加えることで」の意味。"},{"id":5,"original":"Les autorités des deux pays sont par ailleurs toujours sans nouvelles de près de 4 500 personnes.","translation":"また両国の当局は、約4500人について依然として消息をつかめていない。","words":[{"word":"par ailleurs","surface":"par ailleurs","meaning":"そのほか・また","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"sans nouvelles de","surface":"sans nouvelles de","meaning":"〜の消息が不明で","pos":"形容詞句"}],"grammar":"toujours は「いつも」だけでなく、否定的な文脈では「依然として・まだ」を表す。ここでは「まだ連絡が取れない」の意味。"},{"id":6,"original":"L'Union européenne va suspendre à partir de jeudi ses importations de volaille et de bœuf brésiliens, ainsi que d'œufs et de miel, faute de garanties suffisantes de Brasília sur le respect des règles sanitaires européennes.","translation":"EUは木曜日から、ブラジル産の鶏肉と牛肉、さらに卵と蜂蜜の輸入を停止する。欧州の衛生規則の順守についてブラジル政府から十分な保証が得られなかったためだ。","words":[{"word":"suspendre","surface":"suspendre","meaning":"停止する・保留する","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"volaille","surface":"volaille","meaning":"家禽・鶏肉","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"ainsi que","surface":"ainsi que","meaning":"〜と同様に・および","pos":"接続詞句"},{"word":"faute de","surface":"faute de","meaning":"〜がないために","pos":"前置詞句"},{"word":"sanitaire","surface":"sanitaires","meaning":"衛生の","pos":"形容詞"}],"grammar":"faute de + 無冠詞名詞で「〜が欠けているために」という理由を表す。faute de temps（時間がなくて）のように使う頻出表現。"}]},{"metadata":{"issue":"2026-W36","language":"fr","country":"フランス","publishDate":"2026-09-01","targetLanguage":"ja","id":"fr-2026-W36-street-talk","section":"street-talk","kind":"dialogue","title":"« Ils vont l'utiliser en cachette, c'est sûr »","titleJa":"「どうせ隠れて使うって」― 新学期の親たちの本音","leadJa":"高校生の子を持つカミーユと、教員のヤニス。新学期の夕方、パリのカフェでの会話です。教科書のフランス語ではなく、実際に交わされる崩れた話し言葉 ― ouais、du coup、carrément といった相槌や口語表現に注目してください。","category":"生活","level":"中級","trivia":"話し言葉では ne がほぼ落ちます（je ne sais pas → j'sais pas）。また疑問文も「主語＋動詞？」の語順のまま、語尾を上げるだけで済ませるのが普通です。"},"segments":[{"id":1,"original":"Alors, cette rentrée ? Ça s'est passé comment pour Léa ?","speaker":"Yanis","translation":"で、新学期どうだった？レアはうまくいった？","words":[{"word":"Alors","surface":"Alors","meaning":"で・それで","pos":"間投詞"},{"word":"se passer","surface":"s'est passé","meaning":"（事が）運ぶ・起こる","pos":"動詞"}],"grammar":"Ça s'est passé comment ? は話し言葉の疑問文。書き言葉なら Comment cela s'est-il passé ? だが、口語では疑問詞を文末に置く。"},{"id":2,"original":"Bof. Elle est rentrée en râlant à cause du portable.","speaker":"Camille","translation":"うーん、いまいち。携帯のことでぶつぶつ言いながら帰ってきたわ。","words":[{"word":"Bof","surface":"Bof","meaning":"うーん（気乗りしない相槌）","pos":"間投詞"},{"word":"râler","surface":"râlant","meaning":"ぶつぶつ文句を言う","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"à cause de","surface":"à cause du","meaning":"〜のせいで","pos":"前置詞句"}],"grammar":"en râlant は「en + 現在分詞」のジェロンディフ。「文句を言いながら帰ってきた」と同時進行の動作を表す。"},{"id":3,"original":"Ah oui, l'interdiction au lycée. C'est entré en vigueur aujourd'hui.","speaker":"Yanis","translation":"ああ、高校での禁止ね。今日から施行だ。","words":[{"word":"entrer en vigueur","surface":"entré en vigueur","meaning":"施行される・発効する","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"entrer en vigueur は法律や規則が「効力を持ち始める」ことを表す決まった言い方。ニュースでも会話でもそのまま使う。"},{"id":4,"original":"Franchement, je trouve ça bien. Mais elle, elle est pas d'accord du tout.","speaker":"Camille","translation":"正直、私はいいと思うのよ。でもあの子はまったく納得してない。","words":[{"word":"Franchement","surface":"Franchement","meaning":"正直なところ","pos":"副詞"},{"word":"trouver","surface":"trouve","meaning":"〜だと思う","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"être d'accord","surface":"est pas d'accord","meaning":"賛成である","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"elle est pas d'accord は ne が抜けた話し言葉。書けば elle n'est pas d'accord。また Mais elle, elle... と主語を二重に言うのも口語の特徴。"},{"id":5,"original":"Ouais, j'entends ça toute la journée. Les élèves disent tous la même chose.","speaker":"Yanis","translation":"うん、それ一日中聞かされてる。生徒はみんな同じことを言うよ。","words":[{"word":"Ouais","surface":"Ouais","meaning":"うん（oui のくだけた形）","pos":"間投詞"},{"word":"toute la journée","surface":"toute la journée","meaning":"一日中","pos":"副詞句"}],"grammar":"tous は代名詞として主語 Les élèves を受け、動詞のあとに置かれている。発音は「トゥス」と s を読む点に注意。"},{"id":6,"original":"Et ils disent quoi, du coup ?","speaker":"Camille","translation":"で、なんて言ってるの？","words":[{"word":"du coup","surface":"du coup","meaning":"だから・それで","pos":"副詞句"}],"grammar":"du coup は現代フランス語で最も多用される口語のつなぎ言葉。「その結果」から転じて、軽い「で？」程度の意味で使われる。"},{"id":7,"original":"« Tout le monde va l'utiliser en cachette. » Mot pour mot, ça.","speaker":"Yanis","translation":"「どうせみんな隠れて使うし」って。一言一句そのまま、それ。","words":[{"word":"en cachette","surface":"en cachette","meaning":"こっそり・隠れて","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"mot pour mot","surface":"Mot pour mot","meaning":"一言一句・逐語的に","pos":"副詞句"}],"grammar":"Tout le monde は「みんな」の意味だが文法上は三人称単数扱い。動詞は va（vont ではない）になる。"},{"id":8,"original":"Ha ! Carrément. Et vous faites comment, vous, les profs ?","speaker":"Camille","translation":"はは！まったくね。で、先生たちはどうするの？","words":[{"word":"Carrément","surface":"Carrément","meaning":"まったく・完全に","pos":"副詞"},{"word":"prof","surface":"profs","meaning":"先生（professeur の略）","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Et vous faites comment, vous ? も強勢代名詞 vous を文末に足して「あなたたちのほうは」と対比を出す口語表現。"},{"id":9,"original":"On ramasse les téléphones dans une pochette le matin. Ça prend un temps fou.","speaker":"Yanis","translation":"朝、ポーチに携帯を回収するんだ。ものすごく時間がかかる。","words":[{"word":"ramasser","surface":"ramasse","meaning":"回収する・拾い集める","pos":"動詞"},{"word":"pochette","surface":"pochette","meaning":"小袋・ポーチ","pos":"名詞"},{"word":"un temps fou","surface":"un temps fou","meaning":"とんでもない時間","pos":"名詞句"}],"grammar":"fou は本来「気が狂った」だが、名詞の後ろで「途方もない」という強調に使う。un prix fou（法外な値段）も同じ用法。"},{"id":10,"original":"Je m'en doutais. Vous êtes payés pour ça, maintenant ?","speaker":"Camille","translation":"そうだろうと思った。今はそれも仕事のうちってこと？","words":[{"word":"se douter de","surface":"m'en doutais","meaning":"薄々気づいている","pos":"動詞句"}],"grammar":"se douter de は「〜だろうと察している」。似た形の douter de は逆に「〜を疑う」なので、意味が正反対になる要注意ペア。"},{"id":11,"original":"Ne m'en parle pas. Enfin bon, on verra bien dans un mois.","speaker":"Yanis","translation":"その話はしないで。まあいい、一か月もすれば分かるさ。","words":[{"word":"Ne m'en parle pas","surface":"Ne m'en parle pas","meaning":"その話はやめてくれ","pos":"決まり文句"},{"word":"Enfin bon","surface":"Enfin bon","meaning":"まあいいや","pos":"間投詞"},{"word":"on verra","surface":"on verra","meaning":"様子を見よう","pos":"決まり文句"}],"grammar":"on verra は voir の単純未来。「見てみよう＝そのうち分かる」と結論を先送りするときの定番表現。"},{"id":12,"original":"En attendant, Léa a déjà perdu sa carte de cantine. Ça, c'est la vraie rentrée.","speaker":"Camille","translation":"とりあえず、レアはもう学食のカードをなくしたけどね。これこそ本当の新学期よ。","words":[{"word":"En attendant","surface":"En attendant","meaning":"とりあえず・さしあたり","pos":"副詞句"},{"word":"cantine","surface":"cantine","meaning":"学食・給食","pos":"名詞"}],"grammar":"Ça, c'est la vraie rentrée. のように ça を文頭に出して c'est で受け直すのは、強調のための口語的な語順。"}]}]}]};
